    feat(exec): maker execution lifecycle + opt-in --execution maker (B2b)
    
    Maker (post-only) orders rest across ticks, so add the cross-tick state machine:
    - 'rest' decision action records a working post-only order (not yet owned).
    - working_orders/reconcile_maker_fills/stale_working: a resting order becomes an
      owned 'place' only when its cloid fills; stale quotes get cancelled.
    - cancel_order wrapper in orders.py.
    - femr_tick --execution maker (default 'taker'): refresh fills, promote filled
      quotes, cancel stale, then rest entries post-only instead of crossing the
      spread. Exits stay taker for urgency.
    
    Default stays taker; maker path is opt-in and human-gated. Logic is fully unit-
    tested offline (in-memory DB); first live use should be watched at tiny size since
    exchange calls can't be validated in CI. 69 tests pass, lint clean.

